{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1524206835,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMTYxNDcyMDM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2432","origin":"github"},"title":"Add `--inputs`/`--env` to `run`","message":"Continuing from #2291: It would be very useful to be able to indicate what inputs need to be around for a `run` invocation. It doesn't have to super tailored. Even saying --inputs . to communicate that I want all content to be present for execution would be helpful. A rerun could later on make sure that file that were present back then are available now (not necessarily all files that are present in the current state of the repo.)\n\nLike `--inputs`, `--env` would be useful to have. `run` could use it to capture the respective environment variables, and `rerun` could set or check for conflicting values in the re-execution environment.","files":null}]}